WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.234
-You look fantastic.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.701
Hello and thank you
for coming on the show.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:04.701
-Thanks.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.400
-This is your first time
on the show,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.267
but this is not the first time
I've interviewed you.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.267
-Very true.
-Do you remember this?

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.868
-I do. I actually mentioned it
to your producer.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:13.934
I had no idea.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.033
I was like,
"I've been on the show.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.167
She's like, "No, you haven't."
-Yeah.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.501
This is the truth.
It was 19 years ago.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.601
I found this out.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.968
I guest-hosted for
David Letterman.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.400
I remember I did it.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.000
And you did me such a favor,
because we were friends.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.734
And they were like, "Who --

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.767
do you have any famous friend
that want to come on the show?"

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.067
They couldn't book the show

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:34.667
because I was the host,
and no one really knew me.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.367
So I said,
"Chloë, please help me out."

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:40.567
And Rufus Wainwright --
he helped me out, as well.

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.133
But you came on
and talked with me.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.334
And I have a photo.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.868
This is us 19 years ago on
"David Letterman."

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.234
-Cute!
-Look at us.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:50.767
Buddy...

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.801
Look at us.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.634
-Look, I'm wearing
the same dress.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.634
-You're wearing the same dress.
I mean, look at this.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.901
We could -- Let's re-create it.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.701
I'm trying to
re-create it right now.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.834
Let's do it. Yeah.
Oh, yeah, perfect.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.901
Anyways, I'll never forget that.
Thank you for doing that.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:06.934
-Anytime.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.334
-I mean, we have so much
to talk about.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.100
Congratulations.
You got married.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.267
I'm very --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.634
You actually -- This is your --

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.634
Actually, you got married twice.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.000
-Twice to the same man.
-To the same man. Yeah.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.634
We'll have to get into this,
because this is the first one.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.467
This is your picture here.
This is City Hall.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.200
Congratulations.
-Yes.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.267
-I'm you know, disguising,
with the black dress,

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:31.767
a very large baby bump.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.067
So, yes --
yes, a shotgun wedding.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.267
-Yeah, so you had a
shotgun wedding.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:38.100
This is March 2020.
-Yes.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.734
We did not want to have the
baby out of wedlock.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:42.634
-Yeah. There you go.
So, you did that.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:43.634
How was City Hall?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.267
-Also, there was
a green-card issue.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.334
And love, of course, yeah.
-Of course love.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:49.701
Start with love.
Love first, then green card.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.300
Yeah, not in that order.
Yeah. Of course. Yes.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.734
But then,
when was your second wedding?

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:59.300
-Sunday, a few days ago.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.367
Hey, congratulations.
-I know.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey!

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.000
Look at this. Beautiful.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.968
Look at the gorgeous couple
right there.

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:08.501
Oh, my gosh.
-Yes. 13 years younger.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.234
-I mean -- Ooh, hey.
Watch out. Watch out.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.267
-I'm doing that right.
-Yeah. I'm so happy for you.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.601
I want to talk about
"Girl from Plainville,"

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.234
but I also want to talk about
"Russian Doll,"

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:22.200
because I think when I was
friends with you back then,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.701
we were hanging out with
Natasha Lyonne.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.734
-Yeah, Rufus lived with Natasha.
-That's right!

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.767
-Yes, yes.
And wrote a song for Natasha.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:28.801
-Yes.
-That's right.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.133
-Yeah.
♪ Oh, Natasha ♪

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.400
-Oh, it's beautiful.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.534
But Natasha is now hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.167
-I know. I'll be back here
tomorrow to see her.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.234
I'm going to be in the audience.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.634
First time in
the audience at "SNL."

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:40.133
-You have to.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:43.901
But in this series -- I don't
know if I can say any spoilers.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.734
But you play her mother?

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:46.868
-I play her mother.
-How is that possible?

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.434
-And then she does some
time traveling.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.567
-Okay, gotcha.
Okay, that makes sense.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.067
-Well, I'm her mother
in flashbacks,

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.367
and then she does
some time traveling

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:55.267
and she inhabits my body.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:58.534
So then I had to do, like,
Natasha's Nadia shtick,

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.467
which was very difficult for me.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:05.667
-You do that and then you go
into "The Girl from Plainville,"

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.200
which by the way, oh, my gosh.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.467
You're fantastic in this show.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.567
Congrats.
You're getting rave reviews.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:14.734
It is -- It is a real --
It's a heartbreaking story.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.167
-It's challenging, yes.
-A true story.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.234
-It's a true story.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:18.300
Yeah, it's based on this

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.801
unprecedented
texting suicide case.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.734
And I play Lynn Roy, the mother
of the boy who took his life.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.000
But it was very important to her
that people hear

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.534
her son's story, and she was
really behind the project.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:31.501
So, you know -- Yeah.
-Yeah, I'm glad you did it.

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.934
And you're just so good in it.

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:34.300
And I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.133
Here's Chloe Sevigny and
Elle Fanning in

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.200
"The Girl from Plainville."

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.334
Take a look.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.667
-I miss him.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:43.367
-Me too.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.801
He left you a note, sweetheart.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.834
-Oh. He did?
Well, can I read it?

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:57.834
-Well, I didn't bring it here.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.300
I didn't think it
was appropriate.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.934
-No, no, yeah. Of course.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.834
-Oh, that's how you do it
right there.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:07.133
That is how you do it.
Chloë Sevigny, everybody.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:10.000
"The Girl from Plainville" is
streaming now on Hulu.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.334
Come back whenever you want.

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.467
-I love to.
-I love you, bud.

